  {
   "key": "domains-as-types",
   "ruled": "2026-10-06",
   "cause": "95cba821 (reached main in #72): SCM and SCIM take domain types `dom edom : V -> Type*` instead of domain sizes `V -> Nat` with values in `Fin (dom v)`, and ExoAssignment is `(v : V) -> edom v`.",
   "verdict": "Same models. The examples were re-encoded from a size n to the type Fin n (bits, figDim: 2 to Fin 2; figExo: if v = 0 then 2 else 1 to Fin (if v = 0 then 2 else 1)), so every variable keeps the domain Fin n it had. The mechanisms (figF and the copy chain's) keep their bodies; only their types follow the encoding. Two well-formedness fields changed shape and, at these finite domains, state the same facts: dom_pos (0 < n) became dom_nonempty (Nonempty (Fin n)), and exoProb_sum (a Finset sum of 1) became exoProb_tsum (a tsum of 1, equal to the finite sum by tsum_fintype). The printed types are unchanged because they name bits, figDim and figExo, whose definitions moved. The universe arguments [0] -> [0,0,0] come from the two new Type* parameters.",
